      "Marketing fiber claim is higher than the 1 g on the panel we read"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The value pick if you want organic certification and a greens blend without paying meal-shake prices.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "21 g per 49 g serving (label)",
      "Calories": "150 (label, Vanilla Bean)",
      "Greens on label": "Organic spinach, broccoli, kale",
      "Best for": "Budget organic protein with greens"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "garden-of-life-raw-organic-protein-and-greens",
    "name": "Garden of Life Raw Organic Protein & Greens",
    "brand": "Garden of Life",
    "badge": "Best Low-Calorie",
    "category": "Organic plant protein and greens blend",
    "description": "The lightest true protein-and-greens powder here. It pairs 20 g of protein from organic pea and sprouted grains and legumes with organic spinach, kale, broccoli, alfalfa grass, carrots and beets, plus probiotics and enzymes, per the listing. Retailer labels put it at roughly 100-110 calories per scoop, varying by version and flavor. It is sweetened with organic stevia.",
    "pros": [
